🔍 What Are the Istio Metrics?
The Istio metrics you are seeing (e.g., istio_requests_total) are HTTP request metrics collected by Istio’s sidecar proxy (Envoy).

🛠 Where Do These Metrics Come From?
Every sidecar proxy (Envoy) in your cluster automatically collects and exports metrics about HTTP, gRPC, and TCP traffic.
These metrics are NOT from your application directly—they are from Envoy (which sits between services).
Istio exposes these metrics at http://localhost:15014/metrics for collection by Prometheus.
📌 Types of Istio Metrics
Istio collects both general traffic metrics and sidecar-specific metrics.

Metric Name	What It Tracks	Collected By
istio_requests_total	✅ Total HTTP requests handled by Istio	Sidecar (Envoy Proxy)
istio_request_duration_milliseconds	✅ Time taken to process HTTP requests	Sidecar (Envoy Proxy)
istio_response_bytes	✅ Size of HTTP responses	Sidecar (Envoy Proxy)
istio_tcp_sent_bytes_total	✅ Total TCP data sent	Sidecar (Envoy Proxy)
istio_tcp_received_bytes_total	✅ Total TCP data received	Sidecar (Envoy Proxy)
🛠 How Istio Collects Metrics
A request enters your service mesh
→ Istio’s sidecar proxy (Envoy) intercepts the HTTP request.

Envoy records metrics
→ Envoy logs the request, response time, bytes sent, etc.

Metrics are sent to Istio control plane
→ Istio exposes metrics at localhost:15014/metrics.

Prometheus scrapes the metrics
→ If Prometheus is running, it collects Istio’s HTTP and TCP traffic metrics.

✅ Are These Metrics About Sidecars or Services?
👉 These are HTTP request metrics collected by Istio’s sidecar (Envoy proxy), not directly from your services.

Sidecar → Collects Traffic Metrics → Sends to Prometheus → You Query Metrics

